WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:02.902
To Russia's war now.

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:04.471
And Ukraine says it used

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:05.772
the US made Patriot

00:00:05.772 --> 00:00:07.607
air defense system to intercept

00:00:07.607 --> 00:00:09.209
a Russian hypersonic missile.

00:00:09.209 --> 00:00:10.377
Yeah, this is the first time

00:00:10.377 --> 00:00:11.678
the newly acquired system

00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:13.613
has been used to take down

00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:16.249
one of Moscow's most modern missiles.

00:00:16.483 --> 00:00:17.517
CNN's Sam Kiley

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:19.085
joining us now live from Kiev.

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:19.953
Sam, I mean, this sounds

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:20.887
pretty significant,

00:00:20.887 --> 00:00:24.190
like a big win for Ukraine.

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:27.093
A really big win

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:30.096
or an act of exceptional marksmanship

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:32.365
using a very sophisticated piece

00:00:32.365 --> 00:00:33.333
of weaponry.

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:36.102
All luck and I think that the developers

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:38.371
of the Patriot missile systems,

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:40.006
I mean, particularly the United States

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:40.874
and the Pentagon,

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:41.441
will be looking

00:00:41.441 --> 00:00:42.275
at this incident

00:00:42.275 --> 00:00:44.277
in detail to try to establish

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:46.579
which of those three things it was,

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:48.448
because this is a missile system

00:00:48.448 --> 00:00:50.483
and anti-missile missile system

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:53.420
that was developed to take out missiles

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:54.354
that predate

00:00:54.354 --> 00:00:55.855
the hypersonic

00:00:55.855 --> 00:00:59.426
missile that the Kinzel that the Russians

00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:02.028
have been using occasionally in Ukraine.

00:01:02.028 --> 00:01:02.796
This is a missile

00:01:02.796 --> 00:01:04.464
that the Russians claim can fly

00:01:04.464 --> 00:01:05.832
at ten times

00:01:05.832 --> 00:01:07.133
the speed of sound

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:08.501
in technical terms,

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:10.470
too fast for the Patriot.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:12.205
But the Ukrainians are saying

00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:13.873
that they did successfully shoot

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:14.974
one down now.

00:01:14.974 --> 00:01:15.809
They're very short

00:01:15.809 --> 00:01:18.545
indeed of Patriot missile systems.

00:01:18.545 --> 00:01:19.946
They say they're very short

00:01:19.946 --> 00:01:23.216
indeed of all forms of aerial defenses.

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:25.952
So this has been a major morale booster

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:27.454
for the Ukrainians.

00:01:27.454 --> 00:01:28.788
And it also represents,

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:30.523
from the Russian perspective,

00:01:30.523 --> 00:01:30.790
a bit

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:32.158
of a slap in the face in that

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:33.093
they did assume

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:34.561
that these kinds of missiles,

00:01:34.561 --> 00:01:36.496
although they don't have a large numbers

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:38.231
of them, were pretty invulnerable.

00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:40.066
Now they will have to take

00:01:40.066 --> 00:01:41.134
extra precautions

00:01:41.134 --> 00:01:42.335
to protect those missiles

00:01:42.335 --> 00:01:44.037
that they have been firing.

00:01:44.037 --> 00:01:45.238
Into this country,

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:46.739
and they fire them at a time

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:48.241
when they try to overwhelm

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:49.609
the systems here

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:50.910
with other missiles

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:53.279
and drones from the very primitive

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:55.081
Iranian made showerhead drones

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:57.150
all the way through to the Russian made

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:58.418
cruise missile systems.

00:01:58.418 --> 00:02:01.721
They fight fire swarms of these things.

00:02:01.721 --> 00:02:03.456
And then on top of them, fire

00:02:03.456 --> 00:02:04.991
these hypersonic missiles.

00:02:04.991 --> 00:02:06.993
So it is a significant step

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:07.894
for the Ukrainians,

00:02:07.894 --> 00:02:08.828
but we don't really know

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:10.530
the technical detail whether or not

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:12.732
it was basically a lucky shot.

00:02:12.732 --> 00:02:15.135
Yeah, still some some questions there.

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:16.503
Sam, what do you know about

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:17.303
Russian officials

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:18.938
evacuating civilians

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:20.573
in this area of the region?

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:22.442
This is ahead of an expected counter

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:23.443
offensive.

00:02:23.443 --> 00:02:24.911
The UN's nuclear watchdog

00:02:24.911 --> 00:02:27.347
says they're closely monitoring.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:28.114
What do you know

00:02:32.152 --> 00:02:34.387
Well, Victor, we know from at

00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:36.289
least we know that there are claims

00:02:36.289 --> 00:02:37.924
of these evacuations

00:02:37.924 --> 00:02:39.659
circulating on social media

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:42.462
and being made by the exiled

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:43.530
Ukrainian leadership,

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:45.932
particularly of the town of Melita Paul,

00:02:45.932 --> 00:02:47.467
which is a very important town

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:49.936
to the south of Zakariya

00:02:49.936 --> 00:02:51.137
the town of Zakariya,

00:02:51.137 --> 00:02:52.739
which is still in Ukrainian hands,

00:02:52.739 --> 00:02:53.473
and the Zakariya

00:02:53.473 --> 00:02:54.507
nuclear power station,

00:02:54.507 --> 00:02:55.942
which is in Russian

00:02:55.942 --> 00:02:57.343
hands, essentially multiple,

00:02:57.343 --> 00:02:58.545
has been a bit of a hotbed

00:02:58.545 --> 00:03:01.447
of partizan activity on social media.

00:03:01.447 --> 00:03:02.615
There has been

00:03:02.615 --> 00:03:05.051
images of very large queues of vehicles

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:05.952
leaving the city.

00:03:05.952 --> 00:03:06.953
They've also been

00:03:06.953 --> 00:03:07.820
reports coming

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:09.322
from even Russian officials

00:03:09.322 --> 00:03:10.557
of other towns

00:03:10.557 --> 00:03:13.726
being evacuated closer to the front lines

00:03:13.726 --> 00:03:15.261
in anticipation

00:03:15.261 --> 00:03:18.198
of a Ukrainian offensive along that

00:03:18.198 --> 00:03:18.765
very long

00:03:18.765 --> 00:03:19.499
front line

00:03:19.499 --> 00:03:20.366
there in LA

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:21.935
that essentially runs East-West

00:03:21.935 --> 00:03:23.503
from Aparecida

00:03:23.503 --> 00:03:26.039
all the way through to north of Mariupol,

00:03:26.039 --> 00:03:26.539
which, of course

00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:28.107
was flattened by the Russians

00:03:28.107 --> 00:03:30.243
when they captured it last year.

00:03:30.977 --> 00:03:33.213
This is seen as as preparations

00:03:33.213 --> 00:03:33.746
being made

00:03:33.746 --> 00:03:35.481
by the civilian and Russian

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:38.451
authorities in the south of the country

00:03:38.451 --> 00:03:39.619
that they've captured

00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:40.687
at the beginning of this war

00:03:40.687 --> 00:03:41.854
ahead of a Russian

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:44.557
sorry, Ukrainian offensive in the summer.

00:03:44.557 --> 00:03:45.391
The assumption is

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:47.660
that they will be attacking in the south.

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:48.228
But of course,

00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:49.395
the Ukrainians

00:03:49.395 --> 00:03:49.829
are also

00:03:49.829 --> 00:03:51.097
being trained

00:03:51.097 --> 00:03:55.435
by naito in maneuver warfare and feints

00:03:55.435 --> 00:03:56.402
and fake attacks

00:03:56.402 --> 00:03:57.370
will be very much part

00:03:57.370 --> 00:03:58.838
of any future offensive

00:03:58.838 --> 00:03:59.973
that they do conduct

00:04:02.275 --> 00:04:02.609
All right.

00:04:02.609 --> 00:04:04.244
Sam Kiley, appreciate your reporting

00:04:04.244 --> 00:04:05.878
as always. Thank you.

